  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Eight industrial electromagnet trucks compete for a finite scrapyard of
    real physical metal. ACTION cycles OFF, POSITIVE (red +), NEGATIVE (blue -).
    Opposite poles attract; matching poles repel; neutral steel is attracted by either
    active pole. OFF stops your own field, but other active magnets can still affect
    your truck. Forces fall with distance, respect solid obstructions and have bounded
    force/acceleration; no teleporting magnetic grabs. Pull, push or ram scrap into
    your own colored bay. For controlled hauling, keep the scrap ahead of the magnet
    and reverse toward your bay. The WHOLE object must settle there for1.5seconds
    before its displayed value scores, once. Stored metal is secured and stops responding
    to fields. Barrels1, crates3 and vehicle scrap5points. Highest points at time-up
    wins; ties share placing. Clearing all finite scrap ends the match early. AI
    uses the same fields, real contact, driving and settling rules. Turning sorting
    arms are physical hazards; anchored yard buildings are not loose scrap. Shared/chase/cab,
    free look, Your Crew, weather, horn and optional AI views use collection controls.
    Rematch restores every object. Results offer recorded highlights.
